title: The Ilford North By-election
tags: event
view-if: time >= 3 and time <= 4
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
go-to: win if con_votes >= lab_votes - 2; lose if con_votes < lab_votes - 2

= The Ilford North By-election

The death of the Labour MP for Ilford North has caused a by-election in a classic outer-London marginal. Labour won it by under 800 votes in 1974.

@win
on-arrival: con_mps += 1; lab_mps -= 1; thatcher_rating += 2; loyalist_dissent -= 3
achievement: ilford_north

Vivian Bendall takes the seat for the Conservatives on a swing of nearly 7%. Callaghan's majority grows thinner still.

@lose
on-arrival: thatcher_rating -= 2; loyalist_dissent += 3; wet_dissent += 2

Labour holds the seat. It's a bad night, and some backbenchers start asking whether you can win the big one.
